Identifier	Character	Dialogue	Filename	Line Number	Ren'Py Script
chapter_04_86188994		Day four begins with the sound of someone moving furniture in the apartment above you.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	9	"[what]"
chapter_04_b9560374		You lie still and listen. The scraping goes from one end of the ceiling to the other.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	10	"[what]"
chapter_04_187f33fe		Then it stops directly above your head.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	11	"[what]"
chapter_04_e44efb50		There is no apartment above 3B. The building ends at the roof.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	12	"[what]"
chapter_04_afbaa8bd		You sit up.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	19	"[what]"
chapter_04_ba715838		The bedroom is empty. The closet door is closed. The window is closed.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	20	"[what]"
chapter_04_e842235a		Your phone vibrates in your hand.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	21	"[what]"
chapter_04_b8644912		You do not understand why that is worse.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	24	"[what]"
chapter_04_16f8d3a2		Maya knocks at noon. She is carrying a paper bag, a hammer, and a look you have not seen on her before.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	26	"[what]"
chapter_04_15fa8967	m	I brought food. And a weapon. The food is for me. The weapon is for the door.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	30	m "[what]"
chapter_04_559ba678	e	You think a hammer will help?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	31	e "[what]"
chapter_04_303aa0ae	m	It helps me.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	32	m "[what]"
chapter_04_1132fa39	m	I didn't sleep either. Every time I closed my eyes, I heard your parents' voices.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	33	m "[what]"
chapter_04_8cad6c9f	e	You heard them?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	34	e "[what]"
chapter_04_88d17d33	m	I found a tape in the trash. I thought it was music. It wasn't.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	35	m "[what]"
chapter_04_e4cf02bf	m	They kept saying your name. They kept saying 'take us instead.'	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	37	m "[what]"
chapter_04_294be2d8	e	Stay. Please.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	44	e "[what]"
chapter_04_7a523bae	m	I was hoping you'd ask.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	45	m "[what]"
chapter_04_df53cfbf		She puts the hammer on the kitchen counter and takes off her coat.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	46	"[what]"
chapter_04_0a5951fb	m	We're going to be fine.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	47	m "[what]"
chapter_04_e7975d2c		Neither of you believes it. It helps anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	48	"[what]"
chapter_04_ce3b7327	e	You should go. This isn't your problem.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	54	e "[what]"
chapter_04_ddc3dfa0	m	It became my problem when I found a box of tapes with your name on them.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	56	m "[what]"
chapter_04_4e2ba4e8	m	But fine. If you want to be alone, be alone.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	57	m "[what]"
chapter_04_7f866fb2		She leaves the hammer on the counter.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	58	"[what]"
chapter_04_51bb61b3		The apartment feels smaller after she goes.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	59	"[what]"
chapter_04_ea603297	e	What exactly did they say?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	65	e "[what]"
chapter_04_97570ffe	m	Your mother said they knew what it would cost. Your father said they'd pay it.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	66	m "[what]"
chapter_04_4c02e750	m	Then a voice that wasn't either of them said: 'Seven years. Then he remembers.'	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	67	m "[what]"
chapter_04_cd543d51	e	Seven years.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	68	e "[what]"
chapter_04_83200edb	m	Today is the fourth day.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	69	m "[what]"
chapter_04_e93e8d16		She does not say the rest. She does not have to.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	70	"[what]"
chapter_04_a215d363		Maya sleeps on the couch with the hammer on the floor beside her.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	73	"[what]"
chapter_04_339fad21		You sit in the armchair and watch the hallway door until the light changes.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	74	"[what]"
chapter_04_d3e91ecd		You are alone when the light changes.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	76	"[what]"
chapter_04_1bd36268		The apartment makes its evening noises: pipes, radiators, the soft tick of the building settling.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	77	"[what]"
chapter_04_3fb5c138		Tonight, it sounds like someone practicing your voice.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	78	"[what]"
chapter_04_d7a1f67b		At 2:57 AM, you go into the bathroom to splash water on your face.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	83	"[what]"
chapter_04_af77e342		The bulb above the mirror buzzes. The tap runs brown for a second, then clear.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	84	"[what]"
chapter_04_994ab9d0		You look at yourself.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	85	"[what]"
chapter_04_9b616fa8		Your reflection is a half second behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	91	"[what]"
chapter_04_06264ccc		You raise your hand. It raises its hand.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	92	"[what]"
chapter_04_90b2ce22		You lower it. It keeps its hand in the air.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	93	"[what]"
chapter_04_cac05bf4		Then it smiles.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	94	"[what]"
chapter_04_fbb33dd1		You are not smiling.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	95	"[what]"
chapter_04_786f322d		The glass fogs from the inside.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	100	"[what]"
chapter_04_d0274153		A finger draws letters in the condensation, backward, so you can read them.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	101	"[what]"
chapter_04_4330426f		{i}LET ME OUT.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	102	"[what]"
chapter_04_b45a3b46		The finger keeps moving. It writes the same three words again, smaller, underneath.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	103	"[what]"
chapter_04_ded17c8a		And again.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	104	"[what]"
chapter_04_ded17c8a_1		And again.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	105	"[what]"
chapter_04_ad6f8447		Until the whole mirror is full of them.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	106	"[what]"
chapter_04_1144e510		You stumble back. The mirror is clear.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	112	"[what]"
chapter_04_b26cf946		On the edge of the sink, where there was nothing a moment ago, sits a small brass key.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	113	"[what]"
chapter_04_a213c5b0		A paper tag is tied to it with red thread.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	114	"[what]"
chapter_04_c86a26f3		{i}3B — SERVICE.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	115	"[what]"
chapter_04_a653d27b	m	Ethan?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	124	m "[what]"
chapter_04_91835d8e	m	I heard glass.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	125	m "[what]"
chapter_04_569b41a0	e	It's fine. I'm fine.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	126	e "[what]"
chapter_04_667b5147	m	You're holding a key and staring at a mirror.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	127	m "[what]"
chapter_04_0e8f51b7	m	That's not fine.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	128	m "[what]"
chapter_04_ab293925		From the living room, the hammer falls off the counter.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	130	"[what]"
chapter_04_97fd3499		You are still alone.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	131	"[what]"
chapter_04_3d6b3fcd		Three knocks.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	134	"[what]"
chapter_04_44569138		Not at the front door.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	135	"[what]"
chapter_04_00cb94e6		From inside the wardrobe in the bedroom.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	136	"[what]"
chapter_04_6e1a3a09		The knocking becomes a slow, patient drumming. The wardrobe door jumps in its frame.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	140	"[what]"
chapter_04_8f07bdf8		You cross the bedroom and take the handle.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	147	"[what]"
chapter_04_c0ee5f9d		The wardrobe is cold. The door opens before you pull.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	148	"[what]"
chapter_04_fc49ff58		It is not a coat.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	154	"[what]"
chapter_04_0f96bb95		It is a face made of every face you have ever seen in a mirror.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	155	"[what]"
chapter_04_c61bcbd3		It has your eyes. It has Iris's small hands. It has your mother's mouth.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	156	"[what]"
chapter_04_c1d25fbb		The mouth opens and says your name in your own voice.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	157	"[what]"
chapter_04_94dc510e		You are on the floor. The wardrobe is closed.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	161	"[what]"
chapter_04_d314e05e		There is a handprint on the ceiling above your bed.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	162	"[what]"
chapter_04_a976bd88		It is still warm.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	163	"[what]"
chapter_04_54483d9f		You drag the armchair across the room and wedge it under the wardrobe handle.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	167	"[what]"
chapter_04_2734f936		The drumming stops.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	168	"[what]"
chapter_04_b20e4896		The wardrobe breathes in. The wood bulges outward, once, like a chest.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	169	"[what]"
chapter_04_e12ade8b		Then it settles.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	170	"[what]"
chapter_04_95550d2d		A message arrives.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	171	"[what]"
chapter_04_6847e001		You do not move until the sun comes up.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	173	"[what]"
chapter_04_0dd26753		You shake Maya awake. She is already standing before you finish saying her name.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	179	"[what]"
chapter_04_7e8bda84	m	Where?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	180	m "[what]"
chapter_04_6cef4125	e	The wardrobe.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	181	e "[what]"
chapter_04_4f8e9152		She looks at it for a long time. Then she picks up the hammer.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	182	"[what]"
chapter_04_30a66545	m	Okay.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	183	m "[what]"
chapter_04_921a582a	m	If it comes out, I hit it. If it says something clever, you hit it.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	184	m "[what]"
chapter_04_bf3ac62e		The wardrobe stops knocking.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	185	"[what]"
chapter_04_b3829a27		From inside, very softly, something laughs.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	186	"[what]"
chapter_04_f98f4421		Maya does not lower the hammer.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	187	"[what]"
chapter_04_ad76b7e9		You call Maya. It rings and rings.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	190	"[what]"
chapter_04_29f7ca03		Then she answers, breathless.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	191	"[what]"
chapter_04_0e444807	m	Ethan? What's wrong?	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	192	m "[what]"
chapter_04_8333a96a	e	The wardrobe. It's knocking.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	193	e "[what]"
chapter_04_dc5bbb48		There is a long pause.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	194	"[what]"
chapter_04_c5e74d30	m	Ethan. I'm standing outside your door.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	195	m "[what]"
chapter_04_b3e0fdab		The line goes dead.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	196	"[what]"
chapter_04_a48b9c68		Three knocks. From the front door this time.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	198	"[what]"
chapter_04_ef18f2c5		You do not open it.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	199	"[what]"
chapter_04_313ff3a6		You sit on the edge of the bed with your hands in your lap.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	203	"[what]"
chapter_04_c1c82525		The wardrobe knocks for six minutes. Then it stops.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	204	"[what]"
chapter_04_95550d2d_1		A message arrives.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	205	"[what]"
chapter_04_21f3e11d		You do not sleep.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	207	"[what]"
chapter_04_80913612		Neither does the wardrobe.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	208	"[what]"
chapter_04_96493a63		Your phone lights up before either of you can speak.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	210	"[what]"
chapter_04_660b5f5b		The screen goes dark before you can type anything else.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	218	"[what]"
chapter_04_9a7d0c3d		The message is a promise. You do not know which of you it is for.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	225	"[what]"
chapter_04_3e7e9559		Something breathes against the back of your neck.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	231	"[what]"
chapter_04_9389b6f6	m	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	236	m "[what]"
chapter_04_7ab64fc7	m	The tape. Your parents. The death certificate. The key.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	237	m "[what]"
chapter_04_bc1ad606	m	I think you know what this is.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	238	m "[what]"
chapter_04_5a9ac948	e	Say it.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	239	e "[what]"
chapter_04_279cf5bb	m	I think you died seven years ago.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	240	m "[what]"
chapter_04_c34d750d		The words hang in the air. The apartment does not contradict her.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	241	"[what]"
chapter_04_ee43f0ed	e	I think you're right.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	247	e "[what]"
chapter_04_30a66545_1	m	Okay.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	248	m "[what]"
chapter_04_9793c598	m	Okay. Then we're going to figure out what kept you here, and we're going to unkeep it.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	249	m "[what]"
chapter_04_cd36155d		She sits beside you on the bed. Her shoulder is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	250	"[what]"
chapter_04_fa3305a9	e	I'm right here. I'm alive.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	255	e "[what]"
chapter_04_8a7cbcdc	m	I know.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	257	m "[what]"
chapter_04_b63b7852	m	That's what scares me.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	258	m "[what]"
chapter_04_a980dda1		She does not move away, but something behind her eyes closes.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	259	"[what]"
chapter_04_a90ce0de		At 6:00 AM, the key on the nightstand is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	261	"[what]"
chapter_04_ea6748f4		The wardrobe door is open a finger's width. Inside, there is a seam of darkness that is too straight to be a shadow.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	262	"[what]"
chapter_04_d0d316c6		The hidden room from the blueprint.	game/chapters/chapter_04.rpy	263	"[what]"
chapter_01_a297822e		The cab leaves you on Ashgrove Street with two suitcases and a key that feels older than you do.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	23	"[what]"
chapter_01_1ff684c1		Apartment 3B. Third floor, last door, the one with the paint worn pale around the handle.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	24	"[what]"
chapter_01_986c6957		The agency called it a bargain. They did not call it anything else.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	25	"[what]"
chapter_01_df462033		You were four years old the last time you lived here. You remember the shape of the hallway and nothing that happened inside it.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	26	"[what]"
chapter_01_527a1919		The rooms smell of dust and cold radiators. Boxes crowd the floor like patient animals.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	30	"[what]"
chapter_01_0b6879cc		A couch. A television with no signal. A window that looks onto the brick wall of the next building.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_01_4880d7a0		You tell yourself this is what independence looks like.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	32	"[what]"
chapter_01_e551f829		Something in the kitchen clicks.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	35	"[what]"
chapter_01_5339e132		You wait. Nothing clicks again.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	36	"[what]"
chapter_01_da0a6c6b		You start unpacking. Your hands know where to put things before you do.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	38	"[what]"
chapter_01_9d68c983		The mugs go to the cabinet above the sink. The towels go in the bathroom closet. The photographs go face-down in a drawer.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	39	"[what]"
chapter_01_97cb31fd		You do not remember deciding to put them face-down.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	40	"[what]"
chapter_01_9746caa1		Three knocks at the door. Slow. Polite.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	43	"[what]"
chapter_01_04c7d8ba	m	Hi. Neighbor. 3A.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	46	m "[what]"
chapter_01_7c9b7db5	m	I brought coffee. Well. I brought one coffee. The other one is for me, but I'm willing to negotiate.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	47	m "[what]"
chapter_01_49148046	e	You always greet new tenants with caffeine?	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	48	e "[what]"
chapter_01_3b8d8822	m	Only the ones who look like they slept in a bus station.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	49	m "[what]"
chapter_01_74a781cb	m	I'm Maya.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	50	m "[what]"
chapter_01_3bfdacac	e	Ethan. And yes. Please.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	56	e "[what]"
chapter_01_22d72686	m	Ethan. Good name. Very haunted-house.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	58	m "[what]"
chapter_01_1827116b		She steps inside without being invited, which somehow makes the apartment warmer.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	59	"[what]"
chapter_01_0416fed7	m	I live next door. I make too much coffee and I'm aggressively friendly. You'll get used to it.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	60	m "[what]"
chapter_01_07d7ef9a	e	Thanks. I'm fine.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	66	e "[what]"
chapter_01_b53d7d14	m	You're standing in a room full of boxes holding one lamp like it's a weapon.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	67	m "[what]"
chapter_01_5b1bac77	e	I'm fine.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	68	e "[what]"
chapter_01_c952ea89		She studies you for a moment, then sets the coffee on the floor between you.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	69	"[what]"
chapter_01_21bb7563	m	Okay. I'll be next door if the walls start talking.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	70	m "[what]"
chapter_01_33331465		She smiles like it's a joke. It doesn't sound like one.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	71	"[what]"
chapter_01_ae920b52	e	What do you know about this place?	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	76	e "[what]"
chapter_01_0ac932ce	m	Ashgrove? Old building. Thin walls. Radiators make this noise like someone clearing their throat.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	78	m "[what]"
chapter_01_4e184732	m	Previous tenant left in a hurry. Didn't take the furniture. Didn't leave a forwarding address.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	79	m "[what]"
chapter_01_1ea97b2d	e	Why?	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	80	e "[what]"
chapter_01_ac015e46	m	If I knew that, I'd be charging rent for the story.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	81	m "[what]"
chapter_01_52d7f71f		She looks at the closed bedroom door a little too long.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	82	"[what]"
chapter_01_6698900c	m	One thing. If the phone rings at three in the morning, don't answer it.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	83	m "[what]"
chapter_01_7bd7fff8	e	That's a strange thing to say.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	84	e "[what]"
chapter_01_d3e19834	m	It's a strange building.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	85	m "[what]"
chapter_01_528cce63		The coffee is bitter and too hot. You drink it anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	87	"[what]"
chapter_01_7e9907c5	m	I'll leave you to the boxes. Shout if you need a human being.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	89	m "[what]"
chapter_01_44e2e070		She pauses at the door.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	90	"[what]"
chapter_01_7c3a8f2e	m	Ethan. The phone thing. I wasn't joking.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	91	m "[what]"
chapter_01_b077b755		Maya leaves. The apartment gets larger by exactly one person.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	93	"[what]"
chapter_01_5d58b77d		By late afternoon, the light has gone the color of weak tea.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	98	"[what]"
chapter_01_f6261ee5		You should finish unpacking. Instead you walk through the rooms, touching the walls.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	99	"[what]"
chapter_01_a8e29c52		Before the light disappears, you find a photograph under the window.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	106	"[what]"
chapter_01_ee90f0ec		You do not remember putting it there.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	107	"[what]"
chapter_01_08ba5cb7		You turn it over before you can stop yourself.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	111	"[what]"
chapter_01_5c635a90		The apartment is quiet in the way a held breath is quiet.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	113	"[what]"
chapter_01_8200d185		You make the bed. You check the lock twice. You put your phone on the nightstand and tell yourself you will sleep.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	114	"[what]"
chapter_01_a30417b3		At 2:58 AM, you are awake.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	123	"[what]"
chapter_01_643d75ff		At 2:59 AM, the rain stops.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	124	"[what]"
chapter_01_c67f1591		At 3:00 AM, your phone lights up.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	125	"[what]"
chapter_01_25c7627c		The number is not a number. The screen shows seven zeroes and nothing else.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	130	"[what]"
chapter_01_d3a5bdf8		A photograph arrives.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	131	"[what]"
chapter_01_66aa0461		You do not want to open it. You open it anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	135	"[what]"
chapter_01_10a50246		The photograph is of you.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	141	"[what]"
chapter_01_4fdb9cf4		You are asleep in this bed. Your mouth is open. One hand hangs off the mattress.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	142	"[what]"
chapter_01_7c7b5361		The camera is somewhere above the pillow.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	143	"[what]"
chapter_01_568978ed		There is no one in the room.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	144	"[what]"
chapter_01_c9b945e7		You cross the room without turning on a light.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	151	"[what]"
chapter_01_8bbc5337		The peephole gives you a small, warped circle of hallway.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	152	"[what]"
chapter_01_81572828		The hallway is empty.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	153	"[what]"
chapter_01_91ed786b		Then the circle goes dark. Someone is standing on the other side.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	154	"[what]"
chapter_01_ed492fc2		You do not hear them breathing. You hear yourself breathing, too loud, too fast.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	155	"[what]"
chapter_01_85096c1f		The darkness steps away.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	156	"[what]"
chapter_01_d40a4119		When you look again, the hallway is empty.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	157	"[what]"
chapter_01_ce3b695d		You press call. The line connects before the first ring finishes.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	161	"[what]"
chapter_01_08eb477a	stranger	...	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	162	stranger "[what]"
chapter_01_e5e2c92e	e	Who is this?	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	163	e "[what]"
chapter_01_f4c26a91	stranger	You promised you would come back.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	164	stranger "[what]"
chapter_01_61b69a22	e	I don't know you.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	165	e "[what]"
chapter_01_0f963271	stranger	You will.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	166	stranger "[what]"
chapter_01_1051bd6f	stranger	You have seven days.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	167	stranger "[what]"
chapter_01_cc88d4ed		The call ends. The screen goes black.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	169	"[what]"
chapter_01_e830c533		In the dark, your reflection in the window is still holding the phone to its ear.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	170	"[what]"
chapter_01_429cb13a		You hold the power button until the screen dies.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	174	"[what]"
chapter_01_f2f0ec97		You lie down. You count your breaths.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	175	"[what]"
chapter_01_867b4378		Somewhere in the apartment, a phone rings.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	176	"[what]"
chapter_01_88fa3000		It is not your phone. Yours is dead in your hand.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	177	"[what]"
chapter_01_09085f43		It rings seven times, then stops.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	178	"[what]"
chapter_01_f1de4547		You type: Something is wrong. The phone. My room.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	186	"[what]"
chapter_01_59d4830b		Three dots appear. Then stay.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	187	"[what]"
chapter_01_39cc56e6	m	Don't open the door.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	188	m "[what]"
chapter_01_839d95b5	m	I'm serious, Ethan. Don't open it.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	189	m "[what]"
chapter_01_22a7a8f4		You look at the door. The handle is turning, slowly, one degree at a time.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	190	"[what]"
chapter_01_3f0cd54a		Then it stops.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	191	"[what]"
chapter_01_21f3e11d		You do not sleep.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	192	"[what]"
chapter_01_bdc4e5e3		You put the phone face-down on the nightstand.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	196	"[what]"
chapter_01_21f3e11d_1		You do not sleep.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	197	"[what]"
chapter_01_a31595e8		You sit against the headboard until the numbers on your phone turn to 4:00.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	201	"[what]"
chapter_01_21f3e11d_2		You do not sleep.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	202	"[what]"
chapter_01_33166216		At 3:07 AM, a message arrives from the number with seven zeroes.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	204	"[what]"
chapter_01_d80e7e20		You read it six times.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	206	"[what]"
chapter_01_333ea94c		Then, very softly, from inside the wall behind your bed, someone knocks back.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	207	"[what]"
ch1_wall_adbfef69		The wall is quiet now. That does not mean it has stopped listening.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	253	"[what]"
ch1_wall_4e5c6c6e		Three knocks answer from inside the wall. You have not knocked.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	256	"[what]"
ch1_wall_30134c65		You press your palm to the plaster. It is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	257	"[what]"
ch1_window_5ca8d559		Your reflection is back where it belongs. It watches you from the glass.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	267	"[what]"
ch1_window_878fc829		The window looks onto the brick wall of the next building.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	269	"[what]"
ch1_window_f85db4d7		Your reflection is standing in that wall.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	270	"[what]"
ch1_window_089ff151		You step back. It stays where it is.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	271	"[what]"
ch1_wardrobe_35f9939d		The second lock is still hidden behind the coat rail. The brass keyhole is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	281	"[what]"
ch1_wardrobe_369a51c7		The wardrobe is almost empty. A coat that is not yours. A child's shoebox.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	283	"[what]"
ch1_wardrobe_b6f2767c		Behind the coat rail, a second lock is set into the wood.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	284	"[what]"
ch1_wardrobe_dff368a4		It is newer than the wardrobe. The keyhole is brass.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	285	"[what]"
ch1_nightstand_3f4c7b53		The receipt is still in the drawer. The date has not changed.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	294	"[what]"
ch1_nightstand_2baf222b		The nightstand drawer sticks. Inside, under a dead battery and a takeout menu, is a rent receipt.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	296	"[what]"
ch1_nightstand_5b5ea831		E. Mercer. Apartment 3B. Seven years ago.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	297	"[what]"
ch1_nightstand_f6274834		The agency stamp is the same one on your current lease.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	298	"[what]"
ch1_photo_aac2e592		The photograph is still in your pocket. You can feel the corner of it against your leg.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	307	"[what]"
ch1_photo_d7745b61		The photograph is face-down on the windowsill. The paper is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	310	"[what]"
ch1_photo_e9c3d0e8		You turn it over.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	311	"[what]"
ch1_photo_550ff469		Your parents are standing in front of this building. Your father is laughing at something outside the frame.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	312	"[what]"
ch1_photo_33a30bd7		Your mother has her hand on your shoulder. You are six, maybe seven, missing a front tooth.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	313	"[what]"
ch1_photo_9241f86a		A girl stands beside you. Her face has been scratched away with something sharp.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	314	"[what]"
ch1_photo_17844884		On the back, in your mother's handwriting: Ethan, Iris, 3B. Don't forget.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	315	"[what]"
ch1_photo_23053e95		You do not remember a girl.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	319	"[what]"
ch1_photo_47c5cbc3		You remember the shape of her hand in yours.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	320	"[what]"
ch1_closet_b735fa62		The hall closet is narrow and smells of cedar and old rain.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	326	"[what]"
ch1_closet_959461d1		You find a coat that is not yours. A box of Christmas ornaments. A child's shoe.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	327	"[what]"
ch1_closet_a671e2fc		Then you see the marks on the inside of the door.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	328	"[what]"
ch1_closet_d4f8d76f		Scratches. Hundreds of them. Low down, at the height of a small hand.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	330	"[what]"
ch1_closet_d51cc04e		Someone has carved three words into the wood, over and over.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	331	"[what]"
ch1_closet_f9169065		{i}I'M SORRY. I'M SORRY. I'M SORRY.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	332	"[what]"
ch1_closet_58e1f6bc		Behind you, something exhales.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	338	"[what]"
ch1_closet_7b188e9d		You turn around. The living room is empty.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	339	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_747de3d9		The bathroom mirror is fogged at the edges even though the shower has not run in days.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	345	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_fce19995		You wipe a stripe through the condensation.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	346	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_8824979a		Your reflection wipes a stripe from the other side.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	347	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_e76907a7		You stop moving.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	348	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_385ce674		It does not.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	349	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_effcf6c0		A handprint blooms on the inside of the glass. Small. Fingers spread.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	351	"[what]"
ch1_bathroom_174af6ac		You close the bathroom door and do not look back at it.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	356	"[what]"
ch1_kitchen_cd70f0a7		The old answering machine sits under the wall phone, unplugged.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	362	"[what]"
ch1_kitchen_add61dac		You plug it in. The tape inside begins to turn.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	363	"[what]"
ch1_kitchen_67c53939	mom	Ethan. If you're hearing this, you're already home.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	365	mom "[what]"
ch1_kitchen_681a926e	mom	Don't answer the phone at three. Don't look at the photographs. And don't go into the closet.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	366	mom "[what]"
ch1_kitchen_60d4b55e	dad	We're sorry. We did what we could.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	367	dad "[what]"
ch1_kitchen_530f1170	mom	We love you. Remember that part.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	368	mom "[what]"
ch1_kitchen_62304181		The tape clicks. The message begins again.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	369	"[what]"
ch1_kitchen_67c53939_1	mom	Ethan. If you're hearing this, you're already home.	game/chapters/chapter_01.rpy	370	mom "[what]"
