chapter_05_137251f4		The key fits the wardrobe lock.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	18	"[what]"
chapter_05_9395fe3b		You turn it, and the lock opens with a sound like a small animal waking.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	19	"[what]"
chapter_05_7a65b48c		Behind the coats, the back panel swings inward.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	20	"[what]"
chapter_05_f1f0d7c9	m	I want to say something reassuring.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	25	m "[what]"
chapter_05_ea9a2dae	e	Go ahead.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	26	e "[what]"
chapter_05_13fbb725	m	I've got nothing.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	27	m "[what]"
chapter_05_10c44328		She takes your hand. Her palm is sweating. So is yours.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	28	"[what]"
chapter_05_3c5e5f05		You look at the empty apartment behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	30	"[what]"
chapter_05_c0f914ab		Then you step through alone.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_05_f377e3bd		The hidden room is narrow enough to touch both walls at once.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	36	"[what]"
chapter_05_057df856		It has no windows. The air is cold and completely still.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	37	"[what]"
chapter_05_010798e2		Someone has drawn a circle on the floor in faded red paint. Inside the circle, seven small handprints.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	38	"[what]"
chapter_05_f4c2857e		On the far wall, a wooden shelf holds a tape recorder, a red diary, a row of photographs, and the music box.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	39	"[what]"
chapter_05_e4a4a890		Above the shelf, seven names are carved into the plaster.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	40	"[what]"
chapter_05_118e0b58		The seventh is yours.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	41	"[what]"
chapter_05_c5780f3f		You have the feeling of stepping into a photograph that has been waiting for you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	47	"[what]"
chapter_05_9a0bfaf3		The room is smaller than the blueprint said. The walls are closer.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	48	"[what]"
chapter_05_72ca6d07		The music box is on a low table in the center of the circle. Its lid is closed.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	49	"[what]"
chapter_05_12902d64		The tape recorder is already running.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	50	"[what]"
chapter_05_190e90aa		The tape recorder clicks. Your father's voice fills the room.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	55	"[what]"
chapter_05_7184492f		You cannot make yourself stop listening.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	59	"[what]"
chapter_05_61b399e6		The red diary falls open at your feet.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	62	"[what]"
chapter_05_d708885b		The last page is written in careful, looping letters.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	66	"[what]"
chapter_05_3438eb18		When the tape ends, the room is so quiet you can hear the house settling around you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	68	"[what]"
chapter_05_ea79d55e		Then the music box opens by itself.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	69	"[what]"
chapter_05_e1c6b2a7		Three notes. Three more. The same melody from the basement.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	72	"[what]"
chapter_05_3591e993		Iris is standing inside the circle. You did not see her arrive.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	73	"[what]"
chapter_05_ef5210d5	i	You found it.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	77	i "[what]"
chapter_05_e6fdbfa3	e	The hidden room?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	78	e "[what]"
chapter_05_d25e2097	i	The part of the story where you stop pretending.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	79	i "[what]"
chapter_05_871429b2		She looks at the music box.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	81	"[what]"
chapter_05_430869f6	i	That was mine. The matron took it when she locked me in here.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	82	i "[what]"
chapter_05_642aee9a	i	She said music made me selfish.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	83	i "[what]"
chapter_05_781b0042	i	I only wanted to hear something besides the pipes.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	84	i "[what]"
chapter_05_b0c735aa		Maya makes a small sound behind you. Iris does not look at her.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	86	"[what]"
chapter_05_e80b423c	i	He's been using your parents' voices. He's been using mine.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	87	i "[what]"
chapter_05_1d4fe5ec	i	He can't make a voice of his own. That's why he needs you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	88	i "[what]"
chapter_05_6772382f	e	Why me?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	89	e "[what]"
chapter_05_92ca898c	i	Because you came back.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	90	i "[what]"
chapter_05_23cf071e	i	The others he takes. You he keeps.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	91	i "[what]"
chapter_05_414e04ec		The telephone on the altar rings.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	94	"[what]"
chapter_05_c4ddd11a		It is an old rotary phone, covered in dust. It has no cord.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	95	"[what]"
chapter_05_6933849f		You pick it up.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	96	"[what]"
chapter_05_3d4e64e1	listener	Hello, Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	99	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_844b5fd7	listener	You've grown.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	100	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_d38db011	e	What are you?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	101	e "[what]"
chapter_05_fa8ec578	listener	I am the thing that was already in the room when you were born.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	102	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_91cfc482	listener	The listening. The waiting. The shape behind the door.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	103	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_a1093c7d	listener	Your parents gave you to me for seven years. They thought they could buy you a life.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	104	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_5950ddca	listener	They bought you a delay.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	105	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_e5447007	e	Where are they?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	106	e "[what]"
chapter_05_367febbc	listener	Gone. Mostly.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	107	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_4ed98dd8	listener	They are in the walls. In the phone lines. In the part of you that still expects them to come home.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	108	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_303fd781	listener	If you want to see them, answer the seventh call.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	109	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_024eb9ba	listener	Tomorrow. Three in the morning. I'll be waiting.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	110	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_7e4eb40d		The line goes dead. The dial tone is the sound of someone breathing.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	112	"[what]"
chapter_05_313d13c6	i	Don't listen to him.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	115	i "[what]"
chapter_05_db34bd8e	i	He tells the truth the way a hook tells the truth about water.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	116	i "[what]"
chapter_05_dd46982b	i	The box is the lock. Your blood is the key. My name is the door.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	117	i "[what]"
chapter_05_670ca51c	i	If you play it, you'll remember everything.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	118	i "[what]"
chapter_05_fd358749	i	If you break it, you'll close the door.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	119	i "[what]"
chapter_05_d95d7ef0	i	But a door that closes can't be opened again.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	120	i "[what]"
chapter_05_790dcb0b		You wind the box. The dancer turns.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	131	"[what]"
chapter_05_bd37fa34		The room changes around you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	132	"[what]"
chapter_05_c2e8f7f9		You are seven years old. The wall is open. Iris is on the other side, crying.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	133	"[what]"
chapter_05_0553e94f		You can hear the fire above you. You can hear your mother screaming your name.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	134	"[what]"
chapter_05_d141beae		You put your hand through the gap. Iris reaches for it.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	135	"[what]"
chapter_05_f64ce605		The door slams shut.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	136	"[what]"
chapter_05_25f48d46		You run.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	137	"[what]"
chapter_05_04d245cd		You tell yourself you went for help. You tell yourself the door was locked.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	138	"[what]"
chapter_05_116455d6		You know both things are lies.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	139	"[what]"
chapter_05_6a943f6a		You come back to the hidden room with your face wet.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	143	"[what]"
chapter_05_4afb8a3d	i	There you are.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	144	i "[what]"
chapter_05_ce602cda	i	I've been waiting for you to look at that.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	145	i "[what]"
chapter_05_50ed6058	i	You were a child. He was already here. None of it was your fault.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	147	i "[what]"
chapter_05_f0f33d65	i	But he uses the not-your-fault like a door.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	148	i "[what]"
chapter_05_9beda4c4		Maya's hand finds yours. She does not let go.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	149	"[what]"
chapter_05_b1f9df00		You bring the music box down against the floor.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	157	"[what]"
chapter_05_3c27467b		The wood splits. The dancer snaps in half.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	160	"[what]"
chapter_05_5b2e0800		Something screams inside the walls. Not a person. A room.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	161	"[what]"
chapter_05_116f0386	i	No—	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	162	i "[what]"
chapter_05_6e192ab8		Iris flickers like a bad signal.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	163	"[what]"
chapter_05_002642b8		The phone on the altar rings once, very loud, and then melts.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	164	"[what]"
chapter_05_71d28342	i	You closed it. You closed it before you remembered.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	166	i "[what]"
chapter_05_a7e98e1c	i	That's all right. That's all right.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	167	i "[what]"
chapter_05_4000daa5		She is crying. You do not know if ghosts can cry.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	168	"[what]"
chapter_05_87519114		The room goes dark.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	169	"[what]"
chapter_05_d5badf40		You pick up the music box. It is warm, as if someone has been holding it.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	175	"[what]"
chapter_05_f339817b	i	You're going to have to choose eventually.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	176	i "[what]"
chapter_05_bd1661fc	e	I know.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	177	e "[what]"
chapter_05_2a9ec433	i	No. You don't.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	178	i "[what]"
chapter_05_f9417aab	i	He'll make you think you have more time.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	179	i "[what]"
chapter_05_6a4933f7		She steps aside. The circle on the floor remains unbroken.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	180	"[what]"
chapter_05_64f8e1ad		The memory sits in you like a swallowed stone.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	188	"[what]"
chapter_05_41793e6f		You can feel Iris through the wall. You can feel the fire. You can feel the exact moment you decided to run.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	189	"[what]"
chapter_05_81af6942		The broken music box is still in your hands. The melody is gone.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	191	"[what]"
chapter_05_07b5da72		You can still hear it in your teeth.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	192	"[what]"
chapter_05_17ce600c		The music box is a small, heavy weight under your arm.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	194	"[what]"
chapter_05_252a8739		You can feel it ticking, very faintly, like a second heart.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	195	"[what]"
chapter_05_ed2f4a5f	listener	One night left.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	197	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_91556f47		The voice comes from everywhere. From the walls. From the floor. From the inside of your own mouth.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	198	"[what]"
chapter_05_142c7841	listener	Bring the box. Bring the girl. Bring whoever you want to lose.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	199	listener "[what]"
chapter_05_d27328cf		Maya pulls you toward the wardrobe.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	201	"[what]"
chapter_05_a653d27b	m	Ethan?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	205	m "[what]"
chapter_05_54f11db2	m	Your door was open. I heard voices.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	206	m "[what]"
chapter_05_5a011a12	m	What is this room?	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	207	m "[what]"
chapter_05_66c12dfe	m	We need to go.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	210	m "[what]"
chapter_05_981c0b7e	m	Ethan. Look at me. We need to go now.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	211	m "[what]"
chapter_05_a3fe66f4		You look at her.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	212	"[what]"
chapter_05_34846fbd		For a moment, you are almost sure she is real.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	213	"[what]"
chapter_05_5d52d565		You sit on the bedroom floor with the music box between you and Maya until the sun comes up.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	224	"[what]"
chapter_05_ea3cd453		Neither of you says anything.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	225	"[what]"
chapter_05_8d8a3eb9		The wardrobe door stands open behind you. It is not dark inside. It is waiting.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	226	"[what]"
ch5_tape_fe3fb707		The tape has stopped. You can still hear your father clearing his throat.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	248	"[what]"
ch5_tape_d402350a		You press play. The tape hisses for a long time.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	253	"[what]"
ch5_tape_d01e8c1e	dad	We know what it costs.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	254	dad "[what]"
ch5_tape_001dbd5d	mom	We've read the books. We've made the calls. We know.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	255	mom "[what]"
ch5_tape_25242b30	dad	Take us instead. Let him have the years. Let him grow up.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	256	dad "[what]"
ch5_tape_8f98200e		A third voice answers. It is not a voice so much as a room with a mouth.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	257	"[what]"
ch5_tape_0a979d18	listener	Seven years.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	258	listener "[what]"
ch5_tape_5e1e40ce	mom	Seven.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	259	mom "[what]"
ch5_tape_6c817bb9	listener	And when he remembers, he belongs to me.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	260	listener "[what]"
ch5_tape_3c3a3993		Your mother begins to cry. Your father says her name, over and over, like a prayer that has stopped working.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	261	"[what]"
ch5_tape_e0e1b2da		The tape clicks off.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	262	"[what]"
ch5_tape_745008ef		Seven years ago, you were thirteen.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	268	"[what]"
ch5_tape_b67d482f		You are twenty now.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	269	"[what]"
ch5_tape_e8f54823		The math is a hand closing around your throat.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	270	"[what]"
ch5_diary_56650842		The diary is still open. The pages have started to curl at the corners.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	277	"[what]"
ch5_diary_e412430a		The diary is small enough to fit in a coat pocket. The cover is soft with handling.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	280	"[what]"
ch5_diary_b10eae38		Most of the pages are drawings. A girl with a music box. A boy in a window. A door with no handle.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	281	"[what]"
ch5_diary_d708885b		The last page is written in careful, looping letters.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	282	"[what]"
ch5_diary_bffc53a6		{i}The lady says if I am very quiet, the listening man will bring me a friend.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	283	"[what]"
ch5_diary_76ccf79e		{i}I heard a boy through the wall. He said his name is Ethan. He said he would open the door.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	284	"[what]"
ch5_diary_0a1a658f		{i}I am still waiting. I am not angry. I am just very tired of the dark.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	285	"[what]"
ch5_diary_d5026f07		You close the diary. The room feels smaller than it did before.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	290	"[what]"
ch5_photo_fc4078e5		The photograph is still pinned to the wall. You and Iris, side by side.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	297	"[what]"
ch5_photo_c608ac73		A photograph is pinned to the plaster with a rusted nail.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	299	"[what]"
ch5_photo_c1a14eb7		You are six years old, standing in front of a birthday cake. Iris is beside you, holding a paper crown.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	300	"[what]"
ch5_photo_4888a62e		You are both laughing. Her face is not scratched out.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	301	"[what]"
ch5_photo_146595de		On the back, in a child's handwriting: {i}ETHAN + IRIS. BEST FRIENDS. DO NOT FORGET.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	302	"[what]"
ch5_photo_02921a92		You do not remember the birthday. You remember the paper crown.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	305	"[what]"
ch5_photo_f7dac58b		You remember wanting to give it to someone.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	306	"[what]"
ch5_altar_15150932		The altar is still there. The phones are still ringing, one after another, very softly.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	313	"[what]"
ch5_altar_ef379fa5		The altar is a low table covered with a stained white cloth.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	315	"[what]"
ch5_altar_8953cb30		On it: seven old telephones. Six are black. The seventh is red.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	316	"[what]"
ch5_altar_3adee7bf		Each phone has a name written on the handset in silver ink.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	317	"[what]"
ch5_altar_3785a0bc		The red phone has your name.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	318	"[what]"
ch5_altar_44fa129d		Beside it, a candle burns with a flame that gives off no heat.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	319	"[what]"
ch5_altar_b39bcf30		The red phone rings once. You do not answer it.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	322	"[what]"
ch5_altar_dc57d72e		The candle flame leans toward you.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	323	"[what]"
ch5_names_6d97356c		The names are still there. Yours is still last.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	330	"[what]"
ch5_names_7c719346		The names in the plaster are deeper than the ones in the basement.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	332	"[what]"
ch5_names_c8deb649		Six names, with dates. The seventh name has no date.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	333	"[what]"
ch5_names_bae16329		Under your name, someone has carved a sentence in a different hand.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	334	"[what]"
ch5_names_7fa3a582		{i}HE WAS THE ONLY ONE WHO HEARD ME.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	335	"[what]"
ch5_names_4f5011ec		You touch the words. The plaster is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_05.rpy	338	"[what]"
chapter_02_38a2e03f		Morning arrives without asking permission.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	22	"[what]"
chapter_02_aae8c9a3		You have not slept. Your eyes feel like they have been rolled in sand.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	23	"[what]"
chapter_02_865fb978		The phone is on the nightstand, face-up, battery at forty percent. You did not charge it.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	24	"[what]"
chapter_02_4fb5a132		There are three new messages.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	25	"[what]"
chapter_02_def6b34e		You do not open the phone. You get dressed instead.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_02_50345506		The photograph from yesterday is still in your pocket. Iris. 3B. Don't forget.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	32	"[what]"
chapter_02_67173280		You need to know who she is.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	33	"[what]"
chapter_02_0691fb95		Ashgrove Community College is almost empty on a Saturday.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	38	"[what]"
chapter_02_0da7f6e3		The library occupies the basement of the humanities building. The lights buzz. The air smells of paper and old coffee.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	39	"[what]"
chapter_02_3c3774e6		You tell the librarian you are looking for local history. She points you toward the archives without looking up.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	40	"[what]"
chapter_02_26b00c13		You sit at a reading table with a stack of folders and no idea where to begin.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	47	"[what]"
chapter_02_f0da0f8e		Then someone pulls out the chair across from you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	48	"[what]"
chapter_02_b3b83105	m	You look worse than yesterday.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	52	m "[what]"
chapter_02_6983bed6	e	You're following me.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	53	e "[what]"
chapter_02_b98947a0	m	I'm researching a building. You're researching a building. It's called a coincidence.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	54	m "[what]"
chapter_02_85fa549d	m	Also, you left your door unlocked. I checked.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	55	m "[what]"
chapter_02_47c40d96	e	Something is happening in 3B. Messages. Photographs. A girl in the hallway.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	61	e "[what]"
chapter_02_bb1a7171	e	I found a picture of my parents and a girl I don't remember.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	62	e "[what]"
chapter_02_dd9b67c1	m	Okay. That's not the answer I expected.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	64	m "[what]"
chapter_02_396ca627	m	I've been researching Ashgrove for six months. I thought I was the only one who thought it was wrong.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	65	m "[what]"
chapter_02_52ed9025	e	Wrong how?	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	66	e "[what]"
chapter_02_b07959ef	m	Wrong like a word you keep misreading.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	67	m "[what]"
chapter_02_8bb4a823	e	It's nothing. Family stuff.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	73	e "[what]"
chapter_02_71a850d3	m	Family stuff that made you look like a ghost in a cardigan.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	75	m "[what]"
chapter_02_ee615a14	m	Fine. I'll leave it alone.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	76	m "[what]"
chapter_02_12a7f0d7		She does not leave.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	77	"[what]"
chapter_02_606a8445	e	What do you know about 3B?	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	83	e "[what]"
chapter_02_ccc59b14	m	I know the previous tenant left in the middle of the night. I know the landlord won't show the apartment after dark.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	85	m "[what]"
chapter_02_410912d3	m	I know there are seven names in the building records with no move-out dates.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	86	m "[what]"
chapter_02_99775323	m	And I know you're the first person to ask about them who looks like they're on the list.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	87	m "[what]"
chapter_02_b1c31528		She slides a folder across the table. It is warm from her hands.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	88	"[what]"
chapter_02_5cbeeffd		The archive is smaller than it looks.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	90	"[what]"
chapter_02_2cd7048d		You open folders until the words stop making sense.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	91	"[what]"
chapter_02_129286f6		Maya works beside you. She does not ask questions. She does not stop looking at the door.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	92	"[what]"
chapter_02_7fb4efc8		Near the bottom of the stack, a photocopied newspaper page slides free.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	97	"[what]"
chapter_02_4de03ca2		The headline is small. The photograph is smaller.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	100	"[what]"
chapter_02_8b13eba8	m	There's a room here that doesn't appear on the lease.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	104	m "[what]"
chapter_02_0adc3c93	m	The 3B floor plan has a service corridor that was sealed in 1998. Nobody ever removed it from the building.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	105	m "[what]"
chapter_02_4ad1cd76		When you look up, the library has gone quiet.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	109	"[what]"
chapter_02_3db68145		Not empty. Quiet. The way a room goes quiet when everyone is listening to someone else.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	110	"[what]"
chapter_02_9389b6f6	m	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	113	m "[what]"
chapter_02_fdc53d0b	m	The clock says three.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	114	m "[what]"
chapter_02_f6dce537		You look at your phone. It says 3:00 PM.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	115	"[what]"
chapter_02_a35d6563		The lights go out, one row at a time, from the back of the room toward you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	116	"[what]"
chapter_02_467fe4e3		Then they come back on.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	118	"[what]"
chapter_02_7c232dc3		Maya is holding your sleeve.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	119	"[what]"
chapter_02_dd160efb		You take the photograph out of your pocket and place it between you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	125	"[what]"
chapter_02_c33b9254		Maya looks at it for a long time.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	126	"[what]"
chapter_02_9e89ac5f	m	That's my building. That's your mother.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	127	m "[what]"
chapter_02_ac5f1ef5	m	I've seen the girl before. In the hallway. In my dreams.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	128	m "[what]"
chapter_02_d51a3a9b	m	She never has a face.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	129	m "[what]"
chapter_02_afdc504c		You turn the photo over. The words are still there. Don't forget.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	130	"[what]"
chapter_02_8b34deba	m	I don't think that's a suggestion.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	131	m "[what]"
chapter_02_d83149c8		You put your hand over your pocket.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	136	"[what]"
chapter_02_89800976		Maya notices. She does not push.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	137	"[what]"
chapter_02_594b8021	m	Whatever it is, it's already in the room with us.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	138	m "[what]"
chapter_02_9341fcc4		You do not ask what she means.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	139	"[what]"
chapter_02_29a80ebc		The archivist appears at the end of the aisle. She does not look at either of you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	141	"[what]"
chapter_02_9df994f2		She says the library is closing. Her mouth moves a half second after the words.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	142	"[what]"
chapter_02_ba06ea97		Outside, the street is the wrong color. Too blue. Too still.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	148	"[what]"
chapter_02_bb715e2c	m	Come back to mine. We can order something terrible and look at the files.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	151	m "[what]"
chapter_02_17d65aca	e	I should go home.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	152	e "[what]"
chapter_02_f678e2da	m	That's what he wants you to do.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	153	m "[what]"
chapter_02_0617fdd7	e	Who?	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	154	e "[what]"
chapter_02_0a09cc5a	m	I don't know. But he's patient.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	155	m "[what]"
chapter_02_cd33b7f9		You walk home by yourself.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	162	"[what]"
chapter_02_b9533bbc		The city is full of windows. In every one, someone is standing very still.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	163	"[what]"
chapter_02_830ad08f		Maya's apartment is full of plants and half-finished craft projects and a wall of red string.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	171	"[what]"
chapter_02_599bb219		It smells like cinnamon. You sit on her floor and eat noodles out of a paper carton and, for an hour, the phone does not ring.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	172	"[what]"
chapter_02_b8d185b2		By the time you get back to 3B, it is dark.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	179	"[what]"
chapter_02_62ee3767		You lock the door. You check the closet. You leave the bathroom light on.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	180	"[what]"
chapter_02_f3beac96		At 2:59 AM, someone knocks.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	181	"[what]"
chapter_02_da121a40		Three knocks. From the hallway.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	184	"[what]"
chapter_02_7d08731c		Then three more. From inside the apartment.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	185	"[what]"
chapter_02_4c2f1613		Your phone rings.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	190	"[what]"
chapter_02_c14df014		You do not answer it. It rings seven times and stops.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	192	"[what]"
chapter_02_2468bf30		You turn the deadbolt. The door swings inward before your hand touches the handle.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	200	"[what]"
chapter_02_ce22a182		She stands in the hallway with her hands folded in front of her.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	205	"[what]"
chapter_02_474f8301		She is twelve. She has been twelve for a long time.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	206	"[what]"
chapter_02_ea3983a1	i	You left me in the dark.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	207	i "[what]"
chapter_02_61b69a22	e	I don't know you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	208	e "[what]"
chapter_02_7de38f1f	i	Yes, you do.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	209	i "[what]"
chapter_02_861f356a	i	You used to bring me oranges. You said they were the sun, cut into pieces.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	210	i "[what]"
chapter_02_2811725d		Something in your chest folds open. A memory with no pictures.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	211	"[what]"
chapter_02_8f4aad50	i	My name is Iris. You promised you would come back for me.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	212	i "[what]"
chapter_02_cdbff688	e	I'm sorry.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	213	e "[what]"
chapter_02_67e73703	i	Don't be sorry. Be careful.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	214	i "[what]"
chapter_02_848c936a	i	He hears apologies. They taste like invitations.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	215	i "[what]"
chapter_02_08e2ac73	i	Ask Maya what she isn't telling you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	219	i "[what]"
chapter_02_fbca2ea1		When you blink, the hallway is empty.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	220	"[what]"
chapter_02_4179a954		There is a small, wet handprint on the doorframe.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	221	"[what]"
chapter_02_fbb66cd7		You press your eye to the cold brass circle.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	226	"[what]"
chapter_02_7edfa791		She is standing on the other side, close enough that her face fills the whole circle.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	230	"[what]"
chapter_02_46c1cfa9		Her eyes are not looking at the peephole. They are looking at you through the wall.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	231	"[what]"
chapter_02_dbd20a60		She raises one hand and places it against the door.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	232	"[what]"
chapter_02_e1a3d8bf		The door moves inward half an inch. The chain holds.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	233	"[what]"
chapter_02_c6c01d0f		You stumble back. The hallway light flickers under the door.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	236	"[what]"
chapter_02_5212c40e		Then goes out.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	237	"[what]"
chapter_02_ab7da741		You sit on the floor with your back against the couch and your hands over your ears.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	241	"[what]"
chapter_02_ac3d4b01		The knocking stops.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	242	"[what]"
chapter_02_95550d2d		A message arrives.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	243	"[what]"
chapter_02_ea15eb6e		You stay on the floor until the sky turns grey.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	245	"[what]"
chapter_02_5d619aaf		At 3:10 AM, the phone lights up one last time.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	247	"[what]"
chapter_02_267c6596		You read it until the words stop meaning anything.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	249	"[what]"
ch2_trophy_934553e8		The children in the photograph are still arranged in two neat rows. Iris is still at the edge.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	285	"[what]"
ch2_trophy_35b5cb83		The trophy case is cloudy with fingerprints. Behind the brass cups, a photograph has been taped to the glass.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	287	"[what]"
ch2_trophy_eb27ba5e		Two rows of children in front of St. Agnes. Iris Vale stands at the edge, holding a music box.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	288	"[what]"
ch2_trophy_f441910c		Beside her, a boy's face has been scratched out.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	289	"[what]"
ch2_trophy_4074b0a5		You recognize your own shirt.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	290	"[what]"
ch2_poster_0dbef62f		The poster is still hidden behind the newer notices. The red words have not faded.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	300	"[what]"
ch2_poster_f1048d25		A missing-child poster is buried under six layers of club announcements.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	303	"[what]"
ch2_poster_63193c5d		IRIS VALE. AGE 12. LAST SEEN AT ST. AGNES HOME.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	304	"[what]"
ch2_poster_3cec3cf0		The date is the day after the fire.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	305	"[what]"
ch2_poster_d1c7c572		Someone has written across the bottom in red ink: SHE WAS NEVER MISSING.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	306	"[what]"
ch2_locker_66f91df2		The locker is still open. The names are still fresh.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	316	"[what]"
ch2_locker_848f0485		The locker door is dented and hanging open. The inside is empty except for the scratches.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	319	"[what]"
ch2_locker_de280cf5		Seven names. Six have dates beside them.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	320	"[what]"
ch2_locker_0a69da16		The seventh is yours. The scratches are fresh.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	321	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_f9e6c8ed		The photocopy is already in your bag. You can still see the headline when you close your eyes.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	331	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_717f4f15		The newspaper is brittle at the edges. The date is eleven years old.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	334	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_bc897ef0		{i}ST. AGNES HOME FOR CHILDREN — FIRE KILLS ONE, ONE MISSING.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	335	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_1ac72802		The building on Ashgrove Street was a children's home until 2009. The fire started in the basement.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	336	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_67cd532f		A girl named Iris Vale, age twelve, was never found.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	337	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_4131a7e2		The article says the building was scheduled for demolition. It does not say why it wasn't.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	338	"[what]"
ch2_newspaper_b75a0d12		Iris. The name from the photograph.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	341	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_5d83fa15		You have already memorized the crooked little room behind the wardrobe.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	348	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_425cb1f5		The blueprint is wrapped around a cardboard tube. The paper is soft with age.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	350	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_1eb1dd08		Apartment 3B is laid out in clean blue lines: bedroom, bathroom, kitchen, living room.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	351	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_767fa2cc		And then, behind the bedroom wall, a narrow rectangle with no windows and no door.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	352	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_92ec7978		A service corridor. Sealed in 1998.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	353	"[what]"
ch2_blueprint_da71bdc7		Somebody has drawn a question mark inside it in red ink.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	354	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_65854590		You wish the case file had been empty.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	363	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_7c8e9bd2		The grey box is labeled with an apartment number. 3B.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	365	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_cf79c71b		Inside is a fire marshal's report, a death certificate, and a photograph of a burned room.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	366	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_ed0c6abe		The report lists one casualty.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	367	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_5ba7072a		Ethan Mercer. Age thirteen.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	368	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_27509808		You read your own name on the certificate. Then you read it again.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	369	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_f50c86b4		The date of death is seven years ago.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	370	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_36686037		Your heart is beating. You can feel it in your teeth.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	374	"[what]"
ch2_casefile_f2fbcbf2		The certificate is warm. The ink is fresh.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	375	"[what]"
ch2_computer_3e055cb6		You can still see the email in your head. You wish you couldn't.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	382	"[what]"
ch2_computer_af20ccf6		The terminal is old enough to hum. You log into the archive guest account.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	384	"[what]"
ch2_computer_e1fb841b		There is one saved message in the local history folder. It is addressed to you.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	385	"[what]"
ch2_computer_f6437d56		{i}Ethan. If you are reading this, you have started to remember. We are sorry we could not tell you in person. The arrangement was not meant to last this long. Do not let him see you look behind you. — Mom{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	386	"[what]"
ch2_computer_8177f853		The timestamp is six years ago. The sender address no longer exists.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	387	"[what]"
ch2_computer_596bf197		You print the email. The printer produces a blank page.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	390	"[what]"
ch2_computer_5bdefb31		When you look back at the screen, the message is gone.	game/chapters/chapter_02.rpy	391	"[what]"
chapter_03_507e8d39		You wake on the floor with your phone clutched to your chest.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	18	"[what]"
chapter_03_31252b19		The apartment is full of grey light. The door is still locked. The chain is still on.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	19	"[what]"
chapter_03_ec40a869		There is a message from Maya.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	20	"[what]"
chapter_03_305a1dd2		You check the peephole. The hallway is empty, but the little brass circle is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	26	"[what]"
chapter_03_1970497a		You take the photograph out of your pocket and look at the scratched-out face.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	27	"[what]"
chapter_03_2be1513e		Iris.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	28	"[what]"
chapter_03_e29f4c36		You say the name out loud. The radiator knocks once, like a reply.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_03_3342ecb6		The name feels like a stone in your mouth.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	34	"[what]"
chapter_03_ec520734		Maya is waiting in the hallway with a shoebox and a flashlight.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	38	"[what]"
chapter_03_87ba8f23	m	I went down to the laundry room. The door at the end of the hall was open.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	42	m "[what]"
chapter_03_2065aed7	m	It shouldn't be open. It's been painted shut since before I moved in.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	43	m "[what]"
chapter_03_1da720fa	e	What did you find?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	44	e "[what]"
chapter_03_9f111f09	m	Tapes. A box of them. They all have your name on the label.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	45	m "[what]"
chapter_03_01eb181c	m	And a music box. It was playing when I found it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	47	m "[what]"
chapter_03_c848e374	e	Playing what?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	48	e "[what]"
chapter_03_443b79bb	m	I don't know. It stopped when I looked at it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	49	m "[what]"
chapter_03_9881c567	e	There's a girl. Her name is Iris. She was in the hallway last night.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	57	e "[what]"
chapter_03_3b6c7701	e	She says I knew her. She says I promised to come back.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	58	e "[what]"
chapter_03_42b2cd54	m	I believe you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	60	m "[what]"
chapter_03_ad4e3fbd	e	Just like that?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	61	e "[what]"
chapter_03_f57e95b6	m	I've heard her too. I thought I was losing my mind.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	62	m "[what]"
chapter_03_3ca3fcd8	m	It's a relief, honestly. Losing your mind is lonely.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	63	m "[what]"
chapter_03_52485ef4	e	Show me.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	69	e "[what]"
chapter_03_f467f1f2	m	No questions?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	71	m "[what]"
chapter_03_b00dd9b3	e	I'm saving them for the basement.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	72	e "[what]"
chapter_03_ae91d076	m	Good. The basement has better acoustics.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	73	m "[what]"
chapter_03_00acc88b	e	Put it back. Whatever it is, put it back.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	78	e "[what]"
chapter_03_d7a1f32f	m	You think I went down there for fun?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	80	m "[what]"
chapter_03_89fd4706	m	Something is wrong with this building, Ethan. You can pretend it's not happening, but it is.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	81	m "[what]"
chapter_03_f4433b9a		She shoves the shoebox into your hands anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	82	"[what]"
chapter_03_742f5bd3		The door at the end of the hall is open.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	86	"[what]"
chapter_03_ca8dab46		Cold air rises from the stairwell, carrying the smell of wet concrete and something sweet.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	87	"[what]"
chapter_03_2a554898		The stairs go down farther than they should.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	94	"[what]"
chapter_03_bf0aee5d		You count twelve steps. Then twelve more. Then you stop counting.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	95	"[what]"
chapter_03_5069c9d1		Maya's flashlight beam slides over pipes, old laundry machines, a wall of painted-over doors.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	96	"[what]"
chapter_03_105717ae		At the bottom, there is a room that is not on the blueprint.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	97	"[what]"
chapter_03_ad99d46e		The basement is full of abandoned things.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	102	"[what]"
chapter_03_23cff8ca		Chairs stacked like kindling. A piano with no keys. A row of children's coats hanging on a pipe.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	103	"[what]"
chapter_03_13e2f24a		The music box sits on a wooden crate in the middle of the floor, untouched.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	104	"[what]"
chapter_03_b111ed38		Before you leave, the music box begins to play by itself.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	109	"[what]"
chapter_03_93254e5b		A thin, sweet melody. Three notes, then three more.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	111	"[what]"
chapter_03_92e57c6f		One of the drawings falls from the wall and lands at your feet.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	116	"[what]"
chapter_03_37a3d409		A tall figure with no face. A small room. A telephone.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	117	"[what]"
chapter_03_b18c08ab		The basement door slams shut.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	123	"[what]"
chapter_03_513173f6		Maya's flashlight goes out.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	124	"[what]"
chapter_03_9b35b11b		In the dark, someone small is standing beside the piano.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	129	"[what]"
chapter_03_79bd69ef	i	You came down.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	130	i "[what]"
chapter_03_e4d0dcb4	e	Iris.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	132	e "[what]"
chapter_03_d01e2be4	i	You remember my name.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	134	i "[what]"
chapter_03_cdee1518	i	That's more than you did last time.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	135	i "[what]"
chapter_03_eb9edccd	e	Who are you?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	137	e "[what]"
chapter_03_5ab559fd	i	You know who I am. You just don't want to.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	138	i "[what]"
chapter_03_f59e6c31	i	I used to live in the walls.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	143	i "[what]"
chapter_03_f3781373	i	Not this building. The one inside it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	144	i "[what]"
chapter_03_4c5d2562	i	The matron said the listening room was where bad children went to be quiet.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	145	i "[what]"
chapter_03_f6667bc0	i	She was wrong. It was where the quiet went to become a person.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	146	i "[what]"
chapter_03_1bd6a278	e	The Listener.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	148	e "[what]"
chapter_03_8d3fceab	i	You know his name.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	150	i "[what]"
chapter_03_f46d7caa	e	I've heard it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	151	e "[what]"
chapter_03_5b760ca7	i	He's heard you too. That's how it works.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	152	i "[what]"
chapter_03_2d3679b9		Iris walks around the music box without touching it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	154	"[what]"
chapter_03_765ea16d	i	He takes the ones who answer. I answered because I was lonely.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	155	i "[what]"
chapter_03_09b420dd	i	You heard me through the wall. You were little. You promised to open the door.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	156	i "[what]"
chapter_03_b5b940d8	i	You didn't.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	157	i "[what]"
chapter_03_bbda073a		The words land somewhere deep and old.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	158	"[what]"
chapter_03_ce8fd6cf	e	I'm sorry. I was a child.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	163	e "[what]"
chapter_03_3a0ca21f	i	I know.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	164	i "[what]"
chapter_03_9f7325c9	i	He doesn't.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	165	i "[what]"
chapter_03_9389b6f6	m	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	166	m "[what]"
chapter_03_e66ca114		Maya's voice comes from somewhere behind the piano.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	167	"[what]"
chapter_03_710ed762		You cannot see her.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	168	"[what]"
chapter_03_e2486833	i	He uses the sorry ones. It makes them easier to wear.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	169	i "[what]"
chapter_03_7edb14fe	e	How do I stop him?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	174	e "[what]"
chapter_03_40534704	i	You don't.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	175	i "[what]"
chapter_03_2382933f	i	You remember me. You say my name where he can hear it. You close the door he opened.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	176	i "[what]"
chapter_03_4247c092	e	What door?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	177	e "[what]"
chapter_03_d151bba3	i	The one behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	178	i "[what]"
chapter_03_7c80af50		You turn toward the stairs.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	182	"[what]"
chapter_03_7fb1278b	i	Don't.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	183	i "[what]"
chapter_03_49d27599		Your legs do not move.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	184	"[what]"
chapter_03_85afce78	i	He likes it when you run. It means you still think there's somewhere to go.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	185	i "[what]"
chapter_03_09ec9fcb	i	You have four days left.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	188	i "[what]"
chapter_03_96cf2136	i	On the seventh night, he'll call. If you answer, he keeps you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	189	i "[what]"
chapter_03_387e2291	i	If you don't, he takes someone else.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	190	i "[what]"
chapter_03_0617fdd7	e	Who?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	191	e "[what]"
chapter_03_58a78948	i	Whoever is standing closest.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	192	i "[what]"
chapter_03_fffa4373		From behind the piano, Maya says your name.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	193	"[what]"
chapter_03_4c2f1613		Your phone rings.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	195	"[what]"
chapter_03_3bf818b1		The screen says MOM.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	196	"[what]"
chapter_03_91da5b0d	mom	Ethan. Listen to me. Don't look behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	205	mom "[what]"
chapter_03_1d92f814	e	Mom?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	206	e "[what]"
chapter_03_fc430721	mom	He can only move when you're looking at him. He can only speak when you answer.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	207	mom "[what]"
chapter_03_f2e496f2	mom	The music box is the lock. Your father's blood is the key.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	208	mom "[what]"
chapter_03_0f4d80ae	mom	Remember the girl. Say her name where he can hear it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	209	mom "[what]"
chapter_03_5720d8fb	e	Where are you?	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	210	e "[what]"
chapter_03_bd0a727e	mom	We're sorry. We should have—	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	211	mom "[what]"
chapter_03_69d0b486	stranger	That's enough.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	213	stranger "[what]"
chapter_03_6631e67e		The call drops.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	214	"[what]"
chapter_03_435eeae2		The screen goes black. Your reflection is not in it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	215	"[what]"
chapter_03_e943b38f		The message ends there.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	221	"[what]"
chapter_03_b40e0710		A voicemail notification remains on the screen.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	222	"[what]"
chapter_03_e8970163		You play it again. The last word is different each time.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	223	"[what]"
chapter_03_d9a4099d	i	She called you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	226	i "[what]"
chapter_03_ae7f400f	i	She's been calling for six years. You just stopped hearing her.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	227	i "[what]"
chapter_03_21523e24		Iris looks at the music box.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	228	"[what]"
chapter_03_c96d66d3	i	When you're ready, come back. Bring the box. Bring Maya.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	229	i "[what]"
chapter_03_ca1dae11	i	And whatever you do, don't look behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	230	i "[what]"
chapter_03_0e4cbbac		The basement door opens. The staircase is lit by a single bulb.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	235	"[what]"
chapter_03_11f262f9		Maya is standing at the bottom of the stairs, holding her flashlight with both hands.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	236	"[what]"
chapter_03_c7f0d22c	m	I heard her.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	239	m "[what]"
chapter_03_a01348dc	m	I heard all of it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	240	m "[what]"
chapter_03_7a717fad		You do not have to explain. She takes your hand instead.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	243	"[what]"
chapter_03_20717a4b	m	You were talking to someone.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	245	m "[what]"
chapter_03_4b9bb697	m	There's no one there, Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	246	m "[what]"
chapter_03_bb896734		You look at the place where Iris was standing.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	248	"[what]"
chapter_03_bda3f7cd		The floor is dry.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	249	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_35f83f7f		The music box is still on the crate. The lid is open now. You are sure you closed it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	273	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_7c33ef04		The music box is smaller than your palm, made of dark wood and brass.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	275	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_365792fa		Someone has carved three letters into the lid: I.V.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	276	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_de96d128		You open it.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	277	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_a697242b		A tiny metal dancer turns in a circle. The melody is familiar in a way that has no memory attached.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	279	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_da15d4f3		Inside the lid, tucked under the velvet, is a lock of dark hair tied with red thread.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	280	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_97596f48		When the music stops, the dancer is facing you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	283	"[what]"
ch3_musicbox_2415a33c		You close the lid. The melody continues for three more notes.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	284	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_827b9abe		The drawings are still taped to the pipes. You have counted them twice. There are more each time.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	291	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_d07b91e4		There are drawings taped to the pipes in a neat row. Children's drawings, done in crayon.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	294	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_eb0fc334		A tall figure with no face. A room with no windows. A telephone with a long cord that goes into the floor.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	295	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_8aaa81e0		One drawing shows a boy standing outside a door. The boy is labeled ETHAN.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	296	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_c9c0465e		The door is labeled IN HERE.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	297	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_38452505		There are scratch marks drawn over the door. Hundreds of them.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	298	"[what]"
ch3_drawings_080103b2		You take the drawing of the boy. It is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	301	"[what]"
ch3_names_bcae4275		You do not want to read the names again. Your eyes find yours anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	308	"[what]"
ch3_names_ffe921dd		Someone has carved names into the concrete beside the boiler.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	311	"[what]"
ch3_names_aa41acc8		The corner is too dark to read them clearly. You can barely make out the shape of the letters.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	313	"[what]"
ch3_names_3d622b0e		The flashlight beam picks the names out of the concrete.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	316	"[what]"
ch3_names_2c820030		Seven names. The first six have dates beside them.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	317	"[what]"
ch3_names_118e0b58		The seventh is yours.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	318	"[what]"
ch3_names_dfd8fe92		ETHAN MERCER. No date.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	319	"[what]"
ch3_names_b0e17d4d		Below it, in smaller letters, someone has written: {i}HE CAME BACK WRONG.{/i}	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	320	"[what]"
ch3_names_c48625c0		You touch the carving. The concrete is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	323	"[what]"
ch3_piano_d6157912		The piano is still silent. The fingerprints are still there.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	330	"[what]"
ch3_piano_80d6e2b2		The piano has no keys. The wooden strip where they should be is smooth and dustless.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	332	"[what]"
ch3_piano_1d4267b3		Your flashlight finds child-sized fingerprints pressed into the wood above the missing keyboard.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	334	"[what]"
ch3_piano_38a22e85		Someone practiced here for a long time. The prints face the wall.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	335	"[what]"
ch3_piano_498891d9		You can only see the shape of the piano. The flashlight would show you more.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	337	"[what]"
ch3_piano_c88022c7		When you touch the wood, your fingers find small dents arranged like a keyboard.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	338	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_3f2c3bdb		The handprint on the boiler is still there. It has moved six inches to the left.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	348	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_0e7eb355		The old boiler is dead, but the metal is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	350	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_eed02ca4		A handprint is pressed into the rust, small and delicate, as if someone leaned there for a long time.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	351	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_d48c69a6		You put your hand beside it. It fits.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	352	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_366d3db0		From inside the boiler, something breathes in.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	354	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_5b8cbb2a		Then out.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	355	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_cf6af1d3		Then in again, in time with you.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	356	"[what]"
ch3_boiler_8538a0cf		You step back. The breathing keeps going.	game/chapters/chapter_03.rpy	359	"[what]"
chapter_07_4fcdada2		At 2:57 AM, the apartment is completely still.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	10	"[what]"
chapter_07_50d4d40b		The boxes are back. The photographs are face-down. The wardrobe is whole.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	11	"[what]"
chapter_07_7b74946b		It is the apartment you moved into, before you knew what it was.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	12	"[what]"
chapter_07_5a98e48f		You are sitting on the floor with the music box in front of you. You do not remember putting it there.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	13	"[what]"
