chapter_07_63ef8ec1	m	I'm not going anywhere.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	19	m "[what]"
chapter_07_abed9210	e	You should.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	20	e "[what]"
chapter_07_8a7cbcdc	m	I know.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	21	m "[what]"
chapter_07_975da57c	m	I'm still here.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	22	m "[what]"
chapter_07_2a9558af		Maya is not here.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	25	"[what]"
chapter_07_0ee6c59b		You do not know if she is alive. You do not know if the thing in the hidden room left enough of her to be alive.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	26	"[what]"
chapter_07_61764f2e		The apartment feels very large.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	27	"[what]"
chapter_07_f8a5db69		At 2:58 AM, the rain stops.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	29	"[what]"
chapter_07_3df9ee4a		At 2:59 AM, the wardrobe door opens.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	30	"[what]"
chapter_07_67fc7f16		At 3:00 AM, the phone rings.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	31	"[what]"
chapter_07_27b4d293		The screen does not show a number. It shows a name.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	34	"[what]"
chapter_07_53cea239		IRIS.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	35	"[what]"
chapter_07_afc4d491		You do not answer it. You do not need to.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	37	"[what]"
chapter_07_ba7ad142		The voice comes through the speaker anyway.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	38	"[what]"
chapter_07_3d4e64e1	listener	Hello, Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	43	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_03445022	listener	Thank you for coming back.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	44	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_239c9320	e	I never left.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	45	e "[what]"
chapter_07_383c7800	listener	You did. Seven years ago. Your heart stopped in this room.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	46	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_e3a063f4	listener	Your parents called it back. They offered me their lives, and I took them.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	47	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_11af74bb	listener	I gave you seven years. I only want what I'm owed.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	48	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_45438a9f	e	You want me to answer the call.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	49	e "[what]"
chapter_07_53ffa4c4	listener	I want you to choose.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	50	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_430c4668	listener	That's the part I can't do for you. The choosing.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	51	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_c0182ef0	listener	It's the only thing that tastes like anything.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	52	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_bafdad42		Behind the voice, you can hear your parents. They are saying your name, very softly, from a long way off.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	54	"[what]"
chapter_07_3c1f7e65		You can hear Iris breathing.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	55	"[what]"
chapter_07_3eb6ac2c		You can hear Maya's heart, if she is here, beating a little too fast.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	56	"[what]"
chapter_07_642787df		And behind you, the room is breathing too.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	57	"[what]"
chapter_07_2b4f908c	listener	You have one call left.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	59	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_deb42311	listener	Answer it, and I will let the others go.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	60	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_e945810a	listener	Refuse, and I will take whoever is closest.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	61	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_9e6f2ff9	listener	Or run. I do so enjoy it when they run.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	62	listener "[what]"
chapter_07_bcdc4987		The phone is in your hand.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	64	"[what]"
chapter_07_f6a3bd9c		The red receiver is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	65	"[what]"
chapter_07_0f22e3a4		The room waits.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	66	"[what]"
chapter_07_38b315d2		The evidence arranges itself behind your eyes: the photographs, the dates, the seventh name.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	69	"[what]"
chapter_07_d50422a3		You are not guessing anymore.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	70	"[what]"
chapter_07_2d0a4c95		You wrap the red thread around your wrist. It pulls toward the wardrobe.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	73	"[what]"
chapter_07_1dbd7cb4		Your thoughts are not yours anymore. They are white noise with a shape.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	78	"[what]"
chapter_07_007f205d		You lift the receiver before you decide to.	game/chapters/chapter_07.rpy	79	"[what]"
chapter_06_65bfeff2		You lose a day.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	17	"[what]"
chapter_06_15ccb77f		There is no transition. No dream. You close your eyes on day five and open them on day seven.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	18	"[what]"
chapter_06_ce24c427		The clock says 9:00 AM. The date on your phone says you have been asleep for thirty-one hours.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	19	"[what]"
chapter_06_cfbbc934		There are forty-one messages.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	20	"[what]"
chapter_06_26e82b56		The last message was sent from Maya's phone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	29	"[what]"
chapter_06_550d8a08		The text is typed in your handwriting.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	30	"[what]"
chapter_06_751afcf3		Before you can stand, the bedroom folds inward.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	34	"[what]"
chapter_06_fe569be8		You get up. The apartment is wrong.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	39	"[what]"
chapter_06_6c0ad611		The furniture is arranged the way it was when you moved in. The boxes are packed again.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	40	"[what]"
chapter_06_1205abd3		The photograph is face-down on the windowsill. The key is gone from the nightstand.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	41	"[what]"
chapter_06_08e222d0		On the kitchen table, someone has set out two cups of coffee.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	42	"[what]"
chapter_06_8ce9c65e		One is cold. One is still steaming.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	43	"[what]"
chapter_06_49c61b30		You take the steaming cup with you. You do not know why.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	48	"[what]"
chapter_06_ff0ab28d		The hallway is longer than it was yesterday.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	49	"[what]"
chapter_06_b773ffc1		You count doors. 3B. 3A. Then 3B again.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	50	"[what]"
chapter_06_74741f39		You turn around. 3A is behind you, where it should be.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	51	"[what]"
chapter_06_e8a3b325		You check the bedroom. The wardrobe is gone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	56	"[what]"
chapter_06_ebe2bce7		In its place is a smooth stretch of wall with a small brass key taped to it.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	57	"[what]"
chapter_06_725403ad		You take the key. The wall is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	58	"[what]"
chapter_06_f620b2d1		Then you hear Maya's voice through it, saying your name.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	59	"[what]"
chapter_06_d44a3bd7		You press call.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	63	"[what]"
chapter_06_c752752c		It rings once.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	64	"[what]"
chapter_06_9389b6f6	m	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	65	m "[what]"
chapter_06_5720d8fb	e	Where are you?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	66	e "[what]"
chapter_06_456e37d1	m	I'm where you left me.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	67	m "[what]"
chapter_06_f2b0660d	e	I didn't leave you anywhere.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	68	e "[what]"
chapter_06_da6e67ed	m	You did. You just don't remember yet.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	69	m "[what]"
chapter_06_6631e67e		The call drops.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	70	"[what]"
chapter_06_95550d2d		A message arrives.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	71	"[what]"
chapter_06_2197bba9		Maya's apartment is dark.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	82	"[what]"
chapter_06_00dbce86		The plants are dead. The red string has been pulled off the wall and piled in the middle of the floor.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	83	"[what]"
chapter_06_12e2b971		The pile is shaped like a person.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	84	"[what]"
chapter_06_eb1745e9		The phone on her kitchen counter is off the hook. A voice is coming out of it, very small.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	85	"[what]"
chapter_06_9389b6f6_1	m	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	87	m "[what]"
chapter_06_5435afcf	m	Ethan, can you hear me?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	88	m "[what]"
chapter_06_1dc39681	e	Maya?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	89	e "[what]"
chapter_06_91b448e4	m	Don't trust the hallway. Don't trust the door. Don't trust me.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	90	m "[what]"
chapter_06_7e5be565	e	What?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	91	e "[what]"
chapter_06_9d4a5dbf	m	I'm in the room behind the wall. The one with the circle.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	92	m "[what]"
chapter_06_7bac664a	m	He's using my voice. He's been using it since you got here.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	93	m "[what]"
chapter_06_b62e8795		The line clicks.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	94	"[what]"
chapter_06_eceb6dd6		Her phone rings again.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	97	"[what]"
chapter_06_6a892b03		The screen says MAYA.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	98	"[what]"
chapter_06_79b0f91b		You answer.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	99	"[what]"
chapter_06_dd4c8eb2	stranger	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	101	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_7da5dd59		It is Maya's voice, but the words are too slow, as if they are being read from a page.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	102	"[what]"
chapter_06_9f436f35	stranger	Come to the basement. I'm waiting.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	103	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_d2b2da05	stranger	Come alone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	104	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_40cc5095	e	What did you bring to my apartment on day four?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	109	e "[what]"
chapter_06_07e8cb0f	stranger	What?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	110	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_3e6b9f63	e	The hammer, Maya. What did you bring?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	111	e "[what]"
chapter_06_7a8eb4e9		The voice on the other end is silent for a long time.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	112	"[what]"
chapter_06_f7c506ee	stranger	I brought you coffee.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	113	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_cc60c9f0		You hang up.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	114	"[what]"
chapter_06_532feba2		The real Maya would have said the hammer.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	115	"[what]"
chapter_06_575b6e04		You hope she would have said the hammer.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	116	"[what]"
chapter_06_9fcb6d62		You keep the phone to your ear.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	120	"[what]"
chapter_06_52294fb5		The fake Maya breathes. Then stops breathing.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	121	"[what]"
chapter_06_6cbefb53		Then starts again, closer.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	122	"[what]"
chapter_06_97ee903b	stranger	You're standing in my kitchen.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	123	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_cad4dbd8	stranger	You're touching my table.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	124	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_eaac4b9c	stranger	You're so close I can almost wear you.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	125	stranger "[what]"
chapter_06_d44f21d1		You drop the phone. It lands face-up. The screen shows your own face.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	126	"[what]"
chapter_06_a9f3853c		You end the call.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	130	"[what]"
chapter_06_4bf51dbc		The apartment settles around you. Somewhere below the floor, a door opens.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	131	"[what]"
chapter_06_7511ad06		The wall behind the couch is breathing.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	133	"[what]"
chapter_06_020924ce		Two figures are sitting on the couch.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	138	"[what]"
chapter_06_f8e67b67		Your mother. Your father.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	139	"[what]"
chapter_06_aece2352		They are burned. Their faces are the way they looked in the last photograph, before the fire took the details.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	140	"[what]"
chapter_06_1ab11979		They are holding hands.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	141	"[what]"
chapter_06_281937bd	mom	Ethan.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	142	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_43225d2b	dad	You've grown so much.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	143	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_a60efe82	e	You're not real.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	144	e "[what]"
chapter_06_ac64271a	mom	We're as real as you are.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	145	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_385ed8f2	dad	Which is to say: not very.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	146	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_205a1c2a	mom	We did a terrible thing. We made a hole and poured you into it.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	147	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_a887fb57	dad	We thought love was the same as keeping.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	148	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_1e1e2ca9	mom	It isn't.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	149	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_e68e6ee0	dad	The box is the lock. Your blood is the key.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	150	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_294a2e63	mom	The girl is the door.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	151	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_d06cd69d	dad	When he calls tonight, don't answer with words.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	152	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_1ce6e573	mom	Answer with her name.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	153	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_e8be520d		The figures begin to come apart, like ash in a draft.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	154	"[what]"
chapter_06_9ac6a5cd	e	Wait—	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	155	e "[what]"
chapter_06_530f1170	mom	We love you. Remember that part.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	156	mom "[what]"
chapter_06_0320b122	dad	Don't look behind you.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	157	dad "[what]"
chapter_06_efe834a4		They are gone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	158	"[what]"
chapter_06_28d1076f		The room smells of smoke and rain.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	163	"[what]"
chapter_06_f47d039d		The floor beneath the couch is open.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	165	"[what]"
chapter_06_9f15c1ad		A staircase goes down into the dark. It was not there a minute ago.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	166	"[what]"
chapter_06_8dcb4e6c		You go down.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	170	"[what]"
chapter_06_0f35e97c		The stairs are wet. The walls are closer than they were before.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	171	"[what]"
chapter_06_44ae642f		Halfway down, you hear someone counting.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	172	"[what]"
chapter_06_34d5b859		One. Two. Three. Four. Five. Six.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	173	"[what]"
chapter_06_3176ce4c		Then silence.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	174	"[what]"
chapter_06_6bc43b8b		Your heart answers seven.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	177	"[what]"
chapter_06_f3daa40e		The hidden room is lit by the red phone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	183	"[what]"
chapter_06_745072bf		Maya is lying inside the circle. Her eyes are open. She is not blinking.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	184	"[what]"
chapter_06_967f0414		Iris stands over her, one hand held out like she is keeping something back.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	185	"[what]"
chapter_06_6ac828ff	i	You came.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	189	i "[what]"
chapter_06_b8701cfd	e	Is she alive?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	190	e "[what]"
chapter_06_4e4d5709	i	Yes. He's using her to listen.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	191	i "[what]"
chapter_06_ee7c8b6a	i	If you take her out of the circle, he'll have to let go of her.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	192	i "[what]"
chapter_06_7ae820c9	i	If you answer the phone, he'll have you instead.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	193	i "[what]"
chapter_06_934260d6	i	If you break the circle, he'll be angry.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	194	i "[what]"
chapter_06_b042bafc	e	What happens when he's angry?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	195	e "[what]"
chapter_06_f9f92276	i	I don't know. I've never seen anyone survive it.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	196	i "[what]"
chapter_06_a8573d07		The red phone rings.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	198	"[what]"
chapter_06_0ff7276b		Maya's lips move, but the voice comes from the receiver.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	199	"[what]"
chapter_06_6db1f939	m	Ethan. Pick up.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	201	m "[what]"
chapter_06_e369c70d	m	I'm not afraid. Are you?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	202	m "[what]"
chapter_06_68d2ff0a		You step into the circle and take Maya's wrists.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	213	"[what]"
chapter_06_1e867308		She is cold. Too cold. But she is breathing.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	214	"[what]"
chapter_06_dfa8dacf		You drag her across the red paint.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	215	"[what]"
chapter_06_d3e29716		The phone screams.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	216	"[what]"
chapter_06_1096616f		The sound goes through your teeth and out the back of your skull.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	217	"[what]"
chapter_06_7a4ae70c		When it stops, Maya is coughing in your arms.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	218	"[what]"
chapter_06_a653d27b	m	Ethan?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	219	m "[what]"
chapter_06_c4e3360d	m	You look terrible.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	220	m "[what]"
chapter_06_4635653e	e	You're welcome.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	221	e "[what]"
chapter_06_26bdfae7	i	You chose her.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	223	i "[what]"
chapter_06_0cdc1596	i	He didn't think you would.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	224	i "[what]"
chapter_06_31480041		The red phone stops ringing.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	225	"[what]"
chapter_06_5bae218f		You pick up the red phone.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	234	"[what]"
chapter_06_c8bec454	listener	There you are.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	235	listener "[what]"
chapter_06_72f79247	e	Let her go.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	236	e "[what]"
chapter_06_362826b2	listener	Say please.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	237	listener "[what]"
chapter_06_72f79247_1	e	Let her go.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	238	e "[what]"
chapter_06_b22d3b08	listener	You can have her back when you come to me.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	239	listener "[what]"
chapter_06_6bb4a4b1	listener	Tonight. Three o'clock. The seventh call.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	240	listener "[what]"
chapter_06_b3e0fdab		The line goes dead.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	241	"[what]"
chapter_06_2f09c338		Maya's eyes close.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	242	"[what]"
chapter_06_555f5786		Iris kneels beside her and puts a hand on her chest.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	243	"[what]"
chapter_06_d9e3df80	i	She's still here.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	244	i "[what]"
chapter_06_e2fbc5f3	i	But she's very far away.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	245	i "[what]"
chapter_06_fb791971		You cannot tell if that is mercy or a threat.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	246	"[what]"
chapter_06_c2c645f1		You drag your heel through the red paint.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	256	"[what]"
chapter_06_33323283		The circle breaks with a sound like a bone snapping.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	257	"[what]"
chapter_06_60925cf2		Maya gasps. Iris flickers.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	258	"[what]"
chapter_06_1a818353		The red phone rings and rings and rings.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	259	"[what]"
chapter_06_07a230eb		The room tilts. You fall to your knees.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	261	"[what]"
chapter_06_25c456f7		When you look up, Maya is sitting beside you, holding her head.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	262	"[what]"
chapter_06_dc933754	m	What happened?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	263	m "[what]"
chapter_06_e5426ecd	e	I broke something.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	264	e "[what]"
chapter_06_521ca7a8	m	Did it help?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	265	m "[what]"
chapter_06_08dc5581		The phone stops ringing.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	266	"[what]"
chapter_06_2ecd154b		Somewhere above you, a door opens.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	267	"[what]"
chapter_06_1ac6fb50	i	He's coming.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	268	i "[what]"
chapter_06_c911a24b	i	You have until three.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	269	i "[what]"
chapter_06_9b7b3d71	i	The seventh call is not a phone call.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	272	i "[what]"
chapter_06_0fc1b5da	i	It's a choice. He'll make it look like a phone. He'll make it look like me.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	273	i "[what]"
chapter_06_72222d38	i	Don't answer with words. Answer with my name.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	274	i "[what]"
chapter_06_4fb17bfe		Iris begins to fade.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	275	"[what]"
chapter_06_bfbb4ec6	e	Wait. What's your name?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	276	e "[what]"
chapter_06_775d3fc3	i	You know it.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	277	i "[what]"
chapter_06_e4d0dcb4	e	Iris.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	278	e "[what]"
chapter_06_b5ab850d	i	Again.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	280	i "[what]"
chapter_06_bfde6ef9	e	Iris Vale.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	281	e "[what]"
chapter_06_96803af5		She smiles. For a second, she is just a girl.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	282	"[what]"
chapter_06_f93e1ade	i	I'll see you at three.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	283	i "[what]"
chapter_06_a71a7ccb	m	What time is it?	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	295	m "[what]"
chapter_06_296b62c9	e	Almost midnight.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	296	e "[what]"
chapter_06_7074defe	m	Good. We have three hours.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	297	m "[what]"
chapter_06_3ab8a330	m	I'm not leaving you alone with him.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	298	m "[what]"
chapter_06_98ef0c9e		She takes the hammer out of her bag. You do not ask how she got it back.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	299	"[what]"
chapter_06_51d31614		You leave Maya in the hidden room because you cannot carry her and climb at the same time.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	302	"[what]"
chapter_06_8b734827		You tell yourself you will come back.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	303	"[what]"
chapter_06_9a5b53cc		You do not know if it is true.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	304	"[what]"
chapter_06_ce8a758f		Your phone shows seven zeroes.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	308	"[what]"
chapter_06_3f2c26ad		The seventh call is already waiting.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	309	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_3bddfff0		You are standing behind St. Agnes. The trees are bare and very straight.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	326	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_09b34a7e		The burned children's home is a black shape through the branches. Its windows are lit.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	327	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_6c99d772		A red thread runs between the trees, low enough to follow.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	328	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_4a548c8d		Somewhere ahead, a child is counting.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	329	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_c881e13c		Before you wake, the red thread wraps once around your wrist and pulls tight.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	334	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_1417633a		The thread tugs toward the apartment.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	339	"[what]"
ch6_forest_dream_e6c71800		You follow it until the forest folds into the shape of your bedroom.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	340	"[what]"
ch6_forest_carving_4f2b265a		The carved eye is still open. It follows you when you turn away.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	362	"[what]"
ch6_forest_carving_7aa39c60		An eye is carved into the trunk of a black tree. The cuts are old and child-sized.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	364	"[what]"
ch6_forest_carving_58cc470a		Inside the pupil, someone has scratched your initials.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	365	"[what]"
ch6_forest_thread_2efb3289		The red thread is still tied around the branch. It is shorter than it was.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	375	"[what]"
ch6_forest_thread_f78cd2e8		A length of red thread is tied around a black branch.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	377	"[what]"
ch6_forest_thread_4712a825		It runs between the trees and disappears toward Ashgrove Street.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	378	"[what]"
ch6_forest_thread_027b6285		When you touch it, the thread is warm.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	379	"[what]"
ch6_forest_footprints_a1a85644		The footprints are still there. They still do not lead away.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	389	"[what]"
ch6_forest_footprints_b35c4d68		Small bare footprints cross the mud.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	391	"[what]"
ch6_forest_footprints_781590db		They circle the tree, stop at the hollow, and never come out again.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	392	"[what]"
ch6_forest_hollow_cdd2f8e2		The hollow smells of oranges. Something inside it is breathing very slowly.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	402	"[what]"
ch6_forest_hollow_7e3e9e70		A hollow beneath the roots is just large enough for a child.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	404	"[what]"
ch6_forest_hollow_04d7db1f		The wood inside is warm. It smells faintly of oranges.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	405	"[what]"
ch6_forest_hollow_6bd99c92		You do not put your hand inside. You are not sure you could pull it back out.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	406	"[what]"
ch6_survival_46962ced		You keep still. It passes close enough to stir the dust.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	421	"[what]"
ch6_survival_8937e66d		It stops beside you. You hear it deciding.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	427	"[what]"
ch6_survival_538aa79a		Then it moves on.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	428	"[what]"
ch6_survival_23eb5fec		You wait until the basement is completely silent. Then you breathe.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	434	"[what]"
ch6_survival_d0728f53		It finds the edge of your hiding place. It does not find you.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	437	"[what]"
ch6_survival_3eb2d768		When it leaves, you count to one hundred before moving.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	438	"[what]"
ch6_survival_3b9de166		It finds you. For one long second, it wears your face.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	443	"[what]"
ch6_survival_85388f58		Then it is gone, and you are on the stairs with your hands over your mouth.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	444	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_f3d1ebca		You knock on Maya's door.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	453	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_66327d85		It opens inward before your knuckles touch the wood.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	454	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_8dcb4e6c		You go down.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	458	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_6d5c5c5a		The stairs bring you back to the third floor.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	459	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_2e82e9ca		The hallway is exactly as it was. The coffee cup in your hand is hotter than before.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	460	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_53ad18c3		You have not taken a single step.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	461	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_5ffe905d		The elevator arrives immediately.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	465	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_2d6f51c7		The doors open onto a concrete corridor that smells of smoke.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	466	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_cf9b1876		A girl in a hospital gown stands at the far end with her back to you.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	467	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_a0d0d468		She does not turn around.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	468	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_84544dca		The doors close.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	469	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_a5a56ed5		When they open again, you are back in the third-floor hallway.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	470	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_92adf7cd		You stand still.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	474	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_4f2e9a7c		Somewhere behind the wallpaper, someone is counting your breaths.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	475	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_5737add6		You can hear your own name being practiced.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	476	"[what]"
ch6_hallway_0fb34a05		You knock on 3A to make it stop.	game/chapters/chapter_06.rpy	477	"[what]"
ending_truth_6e4c5dd7		You do not turn around.	game/endings.rpy	9	"[what]"
ending_truth_dadf96e0		You say her name.	game/endings.rpy	10	"[what]"
ending_truth_bfde6ef9	e	Iris Vale.	game/endings.rpy	11	e "[what]"
ending_truth_28926387	e	I heard you. I'm sorry. I'm not leaving you in the dark.	game/endings.rpy	12	e "[what]"
ending_truth_0dfaf0ea		The room goes very still.	game/endings.rpy	13	"[what]"
ending_truth_19e9846f	listener	Again.	game/endings.rpy	14	listener "[what]"
ending_truth_bfde6ef9_1	e	Iris Vale.	game/endings.rpy	15	e "[what]"
ending_truth_6b4103b0		You say it until it doesn't hurt.	game/endings.rpy	16	"[what]"
ending_truth_2a8247d7		You say it until it does.	game/endings.rpy	17	"[what]"
ending_truth_b3d636f4	e	I heard you. I was scared. I left you. I'm sorry.	game/endings.rpy	18	e "[what]"
ending_truth_526415c9		The circle on the floor begins to fade.	game/endings.rpy	19	"[what]"
ending_truth_3a0ca21f	i	I know.	game/endings.rpy	20	i "[what]"
ending_truth_7f2b4cc3		Iris steps out of the red paint. For the first time, she looks twelve and tired and free.	game/endings.rpy	21	"[what]"
ending_truth_d769ec89	i	I waited a long time.	game/endings.rpy	22	i "[what]"
ending_truth_bd1661fc	e	I know.	game/endings.rpy	23	e "[what]"
ending_truth_661c0ce0	i	I'm not angry anymore.	game/endings.rpy	24	i "[what]"
ending_truth_8d8a263c	e	You should be.	game/endings.rpy	25	e "[what]"
ending_truth_7da7683c	i	Maybe. But I'm not.	game/endings.rpy	26	i "[what]"
ending_truth_199403b8		Your parents are standing by the wardrobe. They are not burned. They are just your parents, in the clothes they wore in the photograph.	game/endings.rpy	27	"[what]"
ending_truth_281937bd	mom	Ethan.	game/endings.rpy	28	mom "[what]"
ending_truth_4426dfed	dad	We're sorry.	game/endings.rpy	29	dad "[what]"
ending_truth_e9714889	mom	We loved you too much to let you go.	game/endings.rpy	30	mom "[what]"
ending_truth_0b90f10e	dad	We should have let you go.	game/endings.rpy	31	dad "[what]"
ending_truth_bd1661fc_1	e	I know.	game/endings.rpy	32	e "[what]"
ending_truth_f2b17993		You do not know if you forgive them. You know that you are tired of carrying it.	game/endings.rpy	33	"[what]"
ending_truth_282c41fe		The music box opens in your hands.	game/endings.rpy	34	"[what]"
ending_truth_e0cd1880		The melody is small and sweet and terribly brave.	game/endings.rpy	36	"[what]"
ending_truth_86f43213		The Listener makes a sound like a house settling.	game/endings.rpy	37	"[what]"
ending_truth_c7f93c3b	listener	You were mine.	game/endings.rpy	38	listener "[what]"
ending_truth_879634cc	e	No.	game/endings.rpy	39	e "[what]"
ending_truth_f49fd227	listener	You were dead.	game/endings.rpy	40	listener "[what]"
ending_truth_842775fd	e	I was loved.	game/endings.rpy	41	e "[what]"
ending_truth_1b944ab0		The walls go quiet.	game/endings.rpy	42	"[what]"
ending_truth_ba00b411		The phone goes dead.	game/endings.rpy	43	"[what]"
ending_truth_5e429c8b		Your heart slows.	game/endings.rpy	44	"[what]"
ending_truth_7041ec20		Maya is holding your hand when it happens.	game/endings.rpy	49	"[what]"
ending_truth_6e6472f2		You feel her grip tighten. You feel her decide not to let go.	game/endings.rpy	50	"[what]"
ending_truth_27754588		You wish you could tell her it's all right.	game/endings.rpy	51	"[what]"
ending_truth_bea4a141		You hope she knows.	game/endings.rpy	52	"[what]"
ending_truth_2a9558af		Maya is not here.	game/endings.rpy	54	"[what]"
ending_truth_55be9b7f		You hope she is somewhere warm.	game/endings.rpy	55	"[what]"
ending_truth_90c8ee48		At dawn, Maya wakes on the floor of 3B.	game/endings.rpy	60	"[what]"
ending_truth_e1146910		The apartment is empty. The wardrobe is gone. The walls are smooth and white.	game/endings.rpy	61	"[what]"
ending_truth_3719a1d2		On the windowsill, there is a photograph of a boy and a girl at a birthday party. Neither face is scratched out.	game/endings.rpy	62	"[what]"
ending_truth_a15cc9a7		She leaves a cup of coffee there every morning.	game/endings.rpy	63	"[what]"
ending_truth_6d702374		She never answers the phone at three.	game/endings.rpy	64	"[what]"
ending_truth_a79ddf45		The building is demolished in spring.	game/endings.rpy	66	"[what]"
ending_truth_5821d4e9		At the memorial for the children of St. Agnes, there is a new stone with your name on it.	game/endings.rpy	67	"[what]"
ending_truth_2874be47		Under the date, someone has written three words in careful letters.	game/endings.rpy	68	"[what]"
ending_truth_6a3658c5		{i}BELOVED. REMEMBERED. FREE.{/i}	game/endings.rpy	69	"[what]"
ending_truth_422d7e63		You were here.	game/endings.rpy	71	"[what]"
ending_truth_2aec521f		You were loved.	game/endings.rpy	72	"[what]"
ending_truth_370ba3d1		You were not alone at the end.	game/endings.rpy	73	"[what]"
ending_alone_a00c6282		You take Maya's hand.	game/endings.rpy	86	"[what]"
ending_alone_25f48d46		You run.	game/endings.rpy	87	"[what]"
ending_alone_f1f6466a		The hallway stretches. The doors repeat. The carpet turns to water under your feet.	game/endings.rpy	88	"[what]"
ending_alone_732dc1ba		You do not look back.	game/endings.rpy	89	"[what]"
ending_alone_ee334d59		You do not look at the reflections.	game/endings.rpy	90	"[what]"
ending_alone_701afaa0		You do not answer the phone in your pocket, even when it starts to ring.	game/endings.rpy	91	"[what]"
ending_alone_6ea3b9f9		You hit the stairwell. The street. The cold air.	game/endings.rpy	92	"[what]"
ending_alone_fc1556ab		Behind you, the window of 3B is dark.	game/endings.rpy	93	"[what]"
ending_alone_856702a8		You do not stop running until the city is unfamiliar.	game/endings.rpy	95	"[what]"
ending_alone_c16fdf51		Months later, you live in a small apartment with too many locks.	game/endings.rpy	96	"[what]"
ending_alone_73017fcd		Maya sleeps with the light on. You sleep with your back to the wall.	game/endings.rpy	97	"[what]"
ending_alone_adeaa57a		Neither of you talks about the room behind the wardrobe.	game/endings.rpy	98	"[what]"
ending_alone_613262ee		Neither of you has to.	game/endings.rpy	99	"[what]"
ending_alone_1038edfb		At 3:00 AM, a phone rings.	game/endings.rpy	101	"[what]"
ending_alone_76e95139		It is always a phone you do not remember buying.	game/endings.rpy	102	"[what]"
ending_alone_edc34291		You never answer.	game/endings.rpy	103	"[what]"
ending_alone_0bd9fbeb		But sometimes, when Maya is asleep, you listen to the voicemail.	game/endings.rpy	104	"[what]"
ending_alone_c32e7f0d		It is always your voice.	game/endings.rpy	105	"[what]"
ending_alone_9af928da		It says: I'm here.	game/endings.rpy	106	"[what]"
ending_alone_2822391b		You delete it.	game/endings.rpy	107	"[what]"
ending_alone_f9eeb095		It comes back.	game/endings.rpy	108	"[what]"
ending_alone_f15d8f0c		You are never alone.	game/endings.rpy	110	"[what]"
ending_alone_660c8c4c		You were never alone.	game/endings.rpy	111	"[what]"
